{
  "headline": "FDA's records trace our supply to a plant classified OAI 364 days before the posting",
  "headline_cites": ["D6"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "Chloroprocaine hydrochloride has been on FDA's shortage list since 2021-05-17 and as of 2026-10-21 the shortage has been on FDA's list for 65 months.",
      "cites": ["D10"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspection 1123748 at Fresenius Kabi USA, LLC ended 2020-05-18 and was classified OAI with a classification letter dated 2024-05-22, 364 days before FDA posted the shortage on 2021-05-17.",
      "cites": ["D6", "E12"]
    },
    {
      "text": "A second FDA inspection 1174894 at the same Fresenius Kabi USA, LLC facility ended 2022-06-30 and was classified OAI with a classification letter dated 2024-04-30, 409 days after the shortage posting.",
      "cites": ["D7", "E13"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The 20 mg/mL 20 mL presentation used at Corvale East, Corvale General, and Corvale Lakeside carries NDC 00143920910 labeled by Hikma Pharmaceuticals USA Inc. with the manufacturing plant named as HIKMA FARMACÊUTICA (PORTUGAL).",
      "cites": ["E1", "E2", "E4", "E6"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale East holds 30 vials at 3.7 per day for 8.1 days on hand; Corvale Lakeside holds 13 vials at 0.7 per day for 18 days on hand and can spare 2 vials while keeping two weeks of supply.",
      "cites": ["D1", "D3"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The highest-ranked option by rule is to transfer 2 vials of 20 mg/mL 20 mL from Corvale Lakeside to Corvale East, which would raise Corvale East to 9 days on hand and requires a pharmacy director transfer request.",
      "cites": ["D11"]
    }
  ]
}
